 ## Overview
-DDIM Sampling with Classifier-Free Guidance (CFG) is a deterministic (or stochastic) reverse diffusion algorithm that generates samples or refines existing ones by iteratively denoising latent variables while steering the process toward a conditional target [S1, S2, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from standard DDPM sampling by skipping intermediate noise steps to allow for fewer sampling iterations, and by combining unconditional and conditional model predictions via a guidance scale to enhance fidelity [S2, unofficial]. In the context of radiance field optimization, it serves as a denoising mechanism to refine NeRF renderings or guide 3D generation by leveraging 2D diffusion priors [S1, unofficial].
+DDIM Sampling with Classifier-Free Guidance (CFG) is a deterministic (or stochastic with $\eta > 0$) reverse diffusion algorithm that generates samples or refines existing ones by iteratively denoising latent variables [S1, S2, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from standard DDPM sampling by skipping intermediate noise steps to allow for fewer sampling iterations, and by combining unconditional and conditional model predictions via a guidance scale to enhance fidelity [S2, unofficial]. In the context of radiance field optimization, it serves as a denoising mechanism to refine NeRF renderings or guide 3D generation by leveraging 2D diffusion priors [S1, unofficial].
 
